HISTORY_VERSION 1.0.0

TYPE Foundation

STATUS APPROVED

DATE 2026-07-06

TITLE

Ontology 0.1.0 and Instance Contract 0.1.0 defined and written.

WHY

The revised founding roadmap (see the President's 2026-07-06 reorder)
required the .pace/ instance contract to exist before the Kernel, since
the Kernel's job — locate and validate an instance — is meaningless
without an official definition of what a valid instance is. Working
through that definition surfaced a deeper question first: was the
contract about to describe a physical folder structure, or the nature of
the knowledge PACE actually manages? A multi-pass analysis (knowledge
classes, then entities vs. relations vs. assertions vs. representation)
concluded the ontological layer must be defined and written down before
the physical contract, and kept as a separate, more stable artifact that
the physical contract depends on rather than reinvents.

DECISION

Wrote ontology/PACE_ONTOLOGY_0.1.0.pdl, defining PACE's fundamental
categories: ENTITY_TYPES (GOVERNED_UNIT — the same type for a project or
an organization; ACTOR; DECISION; RELEASE; REQUEST; HISTORY_ENTRY),
RELATION_TYPES (BELONGS_TO, SUPERSEDES, IS_CURRENTLY_ACTIVE, DEPENDS_ON,
RESULTS_FROM, PROMOTED_FROM, CITES, ASSERTED_BY/APPROVED_BY), and
ASSERTION_TYPES (HAS_MISSION/HAS_VISION/HAS_ROADMAP/HAS_CURRENT_SPRINT as
one assertion kind at different churn rates, not four; HAS_NAME/HAS_SLUG/
HAS_SCHEMA_VERSION/HAS_CREATED_AT; HAS_CONTINUITY_NOTE as the one
assertion kind that is refined in place rather than superseded).

Wrote contracts/INSTANCE_CONTRACT_0.1.0.pdl on top of that ontology,
defining the physical .pace/ shape: a root INSTANCE.pdl (the GOVERNED_UNIT
entity's identity) and ACTIVE_VERSIONS.pdl (the IS_CURRENTLY_ACTIVE
relation), plus ten sections (mission, vision, roadmap, sprint, history,
releases, decisions, requests, handoff, memory/generated, memory/
persistent) each mapped explicitly to the entity/relation/assertion it
represents, its format, its mutability class, and whether it's required
at v0.1. Per the President's explicit adjustments this same day: sprint
is versioned with an active pointer like mission/vision/roadmap, not
merely mutable; memory is split into generated (regenerable) and
persistent (protected); requests is a new section for the future
Engineering Requests Matrix / Knowledge Intake; handoff stays a mandatory
but empty folder until the Bootstrap/Handoff engine exists; decisions
stays PDL for consistency.

Two mutability classes ended up covering nearly everything (PROTECTED vs
REGENERABLE), with requests/ as the one deliberate exception (protected
core content, but an updatable STATUS/PROMOTED_TO lifecycle field) —
recorded explicitly in the contract rather than left implicit.

IMPACT

PACE now has a written, versioned definition of what a valid .pace/
instance is, grounded in an explicit ontology rather than an ad hoc folder
list. Kernel (the next roadmap step) can be built against this contract
instead of guessing instance shape as it goes.

NEXT_STEPS

Per the revised roadmap: implement a minimal Kernel capable of locating a
.pace/ instance and validating it structurally against
INSTANCE_CONTRACT_0.1.0 (deferring deep/semantic validation to a future
Doctor engine), then a minimal CLI, then pace init, then adopt TuPeríMetro
as the first governed project.

APPROVED_BY

President Cley Duarte

END
